IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `on-pit`

-- Taxation Act, 2007 -- the dated duty: instalments of Ontario tax (s 115 (1) (a), (7)). Kept in its own module so that
-- only this module imports daydate (type-checking with daydate everywhere is slow).
-- © King's Printer for Ontario, 2007. NOT AN OFFICIAL VERSION (see on-pit.l4 and SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `s 115 -- instalments by an individual`

-- Days counted from 1 January of the year (day 0) to a date in that year.
GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER, `day` IS A NUMBER, `month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`days from the start of` `the year` `to` `day` `month` MEANS (Date `day` `month` `the year`) MINUS (Date 1 1 `the year`)

-- s 115 (1): "every individual shall pay to the Ontario Minister in respect of each taxation year, (a) on or before March
-- 15, June 15, September 15 and December 15 in the year, an amount equal to one-quarter of" the estimated tax or the
-- instalment base. s 115 (7): if the individual "is not required to pay instalments ... under section 155 or 156 of the
-- Federal Act by reason of section 156.1 of that Act", subsection (1) does not apply. Whether s 156.1 relieves the
-- individual is a federal question, asked as a fact. The four instalments run together (RAND), each its own act so that one payment cannot discharge two; the amount is not
-- checked.
GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER, `relieved of instalments by ITA s 156.1` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
`the duty to pay Ontario instalments` MEANS
    IF `relieved of instalments by ITA s 156.1`
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE    (PARTY `the individual`
             MUST  `pay the March 15 instalment`
             WITHIN `days from the start of` `the year` `to` 15 3
             HENCE FULFILLED
             LEST  BREACH BY `the individual` BECAUSE "no instalment paid on or before March 15 (s 115 (1) (a))")
        RAND (PARTY `the individual`
             MUST  `pay the June 15 instalment`
             WITHIN `days from the start of` `the year` `to` 15 6
             HENCE FULFILLED
             LEST  BREACH BY `the individual` BECAUSE "no instalment paid on or before June 15 (s 115 (1) (a))")
        RAND (PARTY `the individual`
             MUST  `pay the September 15 instalment`
             WITHIN `days from the start of` `the year` `to` 15 9
             HENCE FULFILLED
             LEST  BREACH BY `the individual` BECAUSE "no instalment paid on or before September 15 (s 115 (1) (a))")
        RAND (PARTY `the individual`
             MUST  `pay the December 15 instalment`
             WITHIN `days from the start of` `the year` `to` 15 12
             HENCE FULFILLED
             LEST  BREACH BY `the individual` BECAUSE "no instalment paid on or before December 15 (s 115 (1) (a))")

-- The same dates as a list: the four s 115 (1) (a) due dates, or none where s 115 (7) applies.
GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER, `relieved of instalments by ITA s 156.1` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
`the Ontario instalment due dates` MEANS
    IF `relieved of instalments by ITA s 156.1`
    THEN EMPTY
    ELSE LIST Date 15 3 `the year`, Date 15 6 `the year`, Date 15 9 `the year`, Date 15 12 `the year`
